    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high-upside production today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.28). **Gunnar Henderson** carries our highest daily efficiency score, buoyed by a favorable matchup against the vulnerable Curry (5.68 xERA), where the combination of plus-skill optimization and a prime batting order position allows him to anchor the offense. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** finds himself in an advantageous spot against Abbott; despite the left-on-left dynamic, the severe mismatch in SP skill projects a massive ceiling, particularly if **Kyle Tucker** can capitalize on run-scoring opportunities from the seventh spot. Both **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.84) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.56) also register as elite starts, with **Jackson Merrill** specifically benefiting from a park factor boost (+14%) that significantly elevates his raw base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Miguel Vargas** on the bench at a 47.59 score. While **Miguel Vargas** remains a viable depth piece, his efficiency was capped by the matchup against the formidable Messick (3.54 xERA) and a lack of platoon leverage. By contrast, **Drake Baldwin** (56.70) and **Coby Mayo** (52.76) were kept in the lineup despite lower scores to ensure we maintain our daily game cap efficiency without sacrificing too much offensive potential. We are monitoring **Nasim Nunez** (39.48) closely, but he remains below our 40.0 floor; his reliance on elite speed makes him a high-variance play, but the combination of Wheeler on the mound and a bottom-order spot renders him a risk we aren't willing to take today. As we look at the remainder of the roster, including **Josh Jung** (52.34) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.91), the focus remains on leveraging the favorable SP matchups against Curry and Adams to gain ground in the 5x5 standings.",
